 Surface events (`user/message`, `assistant/message`, `tool/result`) must declare how they join the ordered surface; raw chunks, boundaries, and other log-only events never produce a message.
 
+At `agent/pre-step`, a policy can append `request/history` with `fromTurn` naming an existing `turn/start` to select that turn and later surface entries for model requests. Appending the event with `{}` restores the full live surface. `requestHistory()` reads the logged selection; invalid turn boundaries are rejected. Selection preserves message roles, tool pairs and archived events, survives replay, and remains in force until another selection. The policy owns the semantic decision; the session does not classify questions.
+
 ### Fork a session
 
 `ctx.sessions.fork(source, boundary?, childSessionId?)` selects source events through an inclusive `boundary` seq (default: the current last event), requires the prefix to end outside an open turn, and creates a live child session with lineage metadata. A tool-time delegation that must branch mid-turn clips to a completed prefix instead.
@@ -128,11 +130,11 @@ The model receives the complete messages from `user/message`, `assistant/message
 
 #### Token effect
 
-Appended surface entries are resent on later steps. A `replace` surface operation removes the shadowed entries from future inputs without deleting their raw log records.
+Selected surface entries are resent on later steps. History selection omits earlier turns without spending a model call or deleting them; restoration includes them again. A `replace` surface operation removes the shadowed entries from future inputs without deleting their raw log records.
 
 #### KV Cache effect
 
-Appended surface entries preserve reusable prefixes. A `replace` operation invalidates reuse from the first shadowed message even though the underlying event log stays append-only.
+Appended surface entries preserve reusable prefixes. History selection or a `replace` operation invalidates reuse from the first changed message even though the underlying event log stays append-only.
 
